      "math_academy_id": "q-71571",
      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "For the function $f(x,y,z)=z-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+3,$ find the equation of the level surface $f(x,y,z)=3.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=3.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ z-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+3 & =3 \\\\ z & ={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surface for $c=3$ is the paraboloid $z={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}.$",
